      { "as": "H1", "text": "Getting Started with React Components" },
      {
        "as": "Lead",
        "text": "Build modern, accessible user interfaces with our comprehensive component library. This guide will walk you through installation, configuration, and best practices."
      },
      { "as": "H2", "text": "Installation" },
      { "as": "P", "text": "To get started, install the package using your preferred package manager:" },
      { "as": "Code", "text": "npm install @invana/ui" },
      { "as": "Muted", "text": "Note: Node.js version 18.0.0 or higher is required." },
      { "as": "Separator" },
      { "as": "H2", "text": "Key Features" },
      { "as": "Large", "text": "Everything you need to build modern applications" },
      {
        "as": "List",
        "items": [
          [{ "strong": "Fully Accessible" }, " - WCAG 2.1 compliant components"],
          [{ "strong": "Customizable" }, " - Tailwind CSS powered theming system"],
          [{ "strong": "TypeScript First" }, " - Complete type safety out of the box"],
          [{ "strong": "Tree Shakeable" }, " - Import only what you need"],
          [{ "strong": "Dark Mode" }, " - Built-in support for light and dark themes"]
        ]
      },
      { "as": "H3", "text": "Performance Optimized" },
      {
        "as": "P",
        "text": "Our components are designed with performance in mind. Each component is optimized for minimal bundle size and maximum runtime efficiency. With lazy loading support and efficient re-rendering strategies, your applications will stay fast even as they grow."
      },
      {
        "as": "Blockquote",
        "text": "\"The best design system I've used. It's fast, flexible, and the developer experience is outstanding. Migration took less than a day for our entire application.\" — Sarah Chen, Engineering Lead at TechCorp"
      },
      { "as": "Separator" },
      { "as": "H2", "text": "Design System Best Practices" },
      { "as": "Muted", "text": "Published on December 22, 2025 • 8 min read" },
      {
        "as": "P",
        "text": "Building a scalable design system requires careful planning and consistent execution. In this article, we'll explore key principles that have helped teams maintain coherence across large applications."
      },
      { "as": "H3", "text": "1. Establish Clear Naming Conventions" },
      {
        "as": "P",
        "runs": [
          "Consistent naming makes your components predictable and easy to discover. Use descriptive names that clearly communicate purpose, like ",
          { "code": "SearchInput" },
          " instead of ",
          { "code": "Input2" },
          "."
        ]
      },
      { "as": "H4", "text": "Component Naming Strategy" },
      {
        "as": "List",
        "items": [
          ["Use PascalCase for component names"],
          ["Prefix composed components (e.g., CardHeader, CardContent)"],
          ["Suffix variants with descriptive terms (e.g., ButtonPrimary, ButtonOutline)"]
        ]
      },
      { "as": "H3", "text": "2. Document Everything" },
      {
        "as": "P",
        "text": "Good documentation is the foundation of a successful design system. Each component should have clear usage examples, prop definitions, and accessibility guidelines."
      },
      { "as": "H4", "text": "Essential Documentation Elements" },
      {
        "as": "P",
        "text": "Every component page should include: interactive examples, code snippets, accessibility notes, and common use cases. This helps developers understand not just how to use a component, but when to use it."
      },
      { "as": "H5", "text": "Interactive Examples" },
      { "as": "Small", "text": "TIP: Live demos with editable code" },
      {
        "as": "P",
        "text": "Interactive examples allow developers to experiment with different props and see results in real-time. Tools like Storybook make this process seamless."
      },
      { "as": "H5", "text": "Code Snippets" },
      {
        "as": "P",
        "text": "Provide ready-to-use code snippets that developers can copy and paste directly into their projects. Include common patterns and edge cases."
      },
      { "as": "H6", "text": "Additional Resources" },
      { "as": "Muted", "text": "Check out our GitHub repository for more examples and community contributions." },
      { "as": "Separator" },
      { "as": "H1", "text": "Build Better Products, Faster" },
      { "as": "Large", "text": "Join thousands of developers who trust Invana UI for their next project" },
      {
        "as": "P",
        "text": "Whether you're building a startup MVP or an enterprise application, our component library scales with your needs. Start shipping features today, not fighting with UI inconsistencies."
      },
      {
        "as": "Metrics",
        "items": [
          { "label": "Weekly Downloads", "value": "50K+" },
          { "label": "Uptime SLA", "value": "99.8%" },
          { "label": "Support Available", "value": "24/7" }
        ]
      },
      { "as": "Blockquote", "text": "Start building today. No credit card required." },
      { "as": "Separator" },
